# P01 application options.

config NU54_DEV_SETUP
	bool "Week-7 fixed setup when no rental setup is stored"
	default y
	help
	  Without a stored rental setup, create the device key at boot and use the operator,
	  settlement contract and chain id from the deployment record (week-7 gate). Turn it off
	  for the rental build: the device then boots UNPROVISIONED and waits for a setup session.

config NU54_REQUIRE_SECURE_SESSION
	bool "Refuse plaintext payment sessions"
	help
	  Payment sessions must open the secure channel (payment-protocol.md 4.1); a plaintext
	  session.open in payment mode is answered with error NOT_PERMITTED. The release build turns
	  it on once the kiosk has the channel; development builds keep plaintext for the week-7 path.

config NU54_REQUIRE_PHONE
	bool "Refuse payments and limit changes with no phone app listening"
	help
	  The renter checks what the device signs on the bonded phone app (payment-protocol.md 3).
	  With this on, payment.prepare and limit.change are refused NOT_PERMITTED when no phone app
	  is listening. Development builds go on without one (week-7 path, N30).

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
